From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:17:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] docs: back up and restore the database in container
 deployments

The backup script needs the sqlite3 command line tool, which the control plane
image does not contain, and the container root filesystem is read-only. Take
the snapshot inside the container with the SQLite backup API, write it to the
data volume and copy it out; restore it the same way from a one-off container
or Pod that mounts the data volume while the control plane is stopped. Writing
the backup through the API lets SQLite handle a leftover -wal of the target.

Also state that the Kubernetes volume must be block storage, since WAL relies
on a shared-memory file and does not work on NFS-like file systems, and that
the Kubernetes manifest keeps a single writer with the Recreate strategy.

Both procedures were exercised against the compose topology and a kind
cluster: resources created after the backup were gone after the restore.
